        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: TechCrunch Disrupt New York 2016\n- Companies: The Honest Company, AOL, Uber\n- People: Jessica Alba, B.J. Novak, Tim Armstrong, David Plouffe\n- Topics: ethical consumerism\n\nFacts:\n- TechCrunch Disrupt New York 2016 included hackathons, investor meet-and-greets, and guest lectures from Jessica Alba, B.J. Novak, Tim Armstrong, and David Plouffe.\n- The Honest Company had $170 million in sales in 2014.\n- As of August 2015, The Honest Company was valued at $1.7 billion.\n- The Honest Company is an American consumer goods company founded by Jessica Alba.\n- The Honest Company emphasizes household products for the ethical consumerism market.\n- At the time of TechCrunch Disrupt New York 2016, Jessica Alba was associated with The Honest Company, B.J. Novak was associated with The Office, Tim Armstrong was associated with AOL, and David Plouffe was a former Obama White House advisor serving on Uber's board.",
